Scaffolded with [devo](https://github.com/Compustretch/devo).

## Run

```bash
cargo run
```

## Local services

```bash
devo services          # see what's available and what's enabled
devo add postgres      # enable a service
devo dev               # start the local stack
devo down              # stop it
```

Enabled services are listed in `devo.yaml`. `compose.yaml` and the files under
`platform/` are generated by devo; edit `devo.yaml` instead of editing them.

## Application lifecycle hooks

Put paired POSIX shell scripts in `scripts/start/` and `scripts/stop/`. For
example, `scripts/start/api.sh` pairs with `scripts/stop/api.sh`. Devo starts
hooks in filename order after Compose services are healthy, and runs stop hooks
in reverse order before removing the Compose stack. Each start hook must return
after launching its application process; redirect long-running process output
to a log file and record its PID so the matching stop hook can stop that exact
process. Hooks must be idempotent: repeated starts must not launch duplicate
processes, and stops should be safe when a process is already stopped. A failed
start triggers stop hooks for attempted applications and tears down the Compose
stack. Existing projects without lifecycle scripts continue to work.
